# Rebuild and reinstall after changes

After any change the user can see in Partly, rebuild and replace `/Applications/Partly.app` before finishing. Do not wait to be asked.

- Compile outside the project, in `/tmp`, so `build/` is not left in the repo.
- Build `PartlyCore` with `-O`. Build the `Partly` app with `-Onone`. Whole-module `-O` has dropped SwiftUI controls from the binary.
- Quit Partly, copy the new app over `/Applications/Partly.app`, then `xattr -cr` it. Ad-hoc sign the bundle.
- Bump `CFBundleVersion`.
- Refresh `~/Desktop/Partly.dmg` as an installer package that replaces `/Applications/Partly.app`. Do not require a drag into Applications.
- Do not commit or push unless the user asks.
